cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "fep_formal: Towards Lean 4 Formalization of the Free Energy Principle"
abstract: >-
  A catalogue of 168 Free Energy Principle topics spanning FEP foundations,
  Active Inference, Bayesian Mechanics, Information Geometry, and
  Thermodynamics. Each row has a canonical Lean 4 topic body, reviewed
  invariant, explicit assumptions, and a separate semantic maturity record.
  The Python package supports deterministic offline artifacts, native
  Lean verification, and configured Hermes/OpenGauss execution. Accepted
  native evidence binds exact source statements to the pinned Lean 4.34.1 /
  Mathlib 4.34.1 workspace with no warnings or proof holes; compilation alone
  does not establish semantic adequacy or empirical validity of the FEP.
